    "answer_zh": "检查太阳能板（开路测试）\n断开太阳能板与TCS3之间的连接，断开各块太阳能板之间的连接，在无遮挡的正午阳光下，测量每一块太阳能板的开路电压\n正常值：>42VDC\n如果某块板明显低于42VDC → 该太阳能板损坏\n检查电池电压\n断开TCS31与电池之间的连接, 测量电池电压\n如果电压 <22VDC → 用外部充电器将电池充到24VDC以上，再重新接入系统\n测试TCS31是否正常（断开太阳能板）\n保持太阳能板断开, 仅连接电池到TCS3, 测量以下端口：\n端口正常值\t                   异常判断\nBAT端口\t= 电池电压; 若异常 → TCS3可能内部BAT通路故障\nLOAD端口>22VDC\t; 若低于22VDC或为0 → UPS01损坏\n如果BAT和LOAD均正常 → TCS3是好的，继续第4步\n接回太阳能板，整体验证\n接回太阳能板到TCS3, 测量以下端口，三者应大致等于电池电压\nSOL端口≈ 电池电压\nBAT端口\t≈ 电池电压\nLOAD端口≈ 电池电压\n如果端口电压异常→ 太阳能板损坏",
    "answer_en": "Check the solar panel(s) – open circuit voltage test\nDisconnect all solar panels from the TCS3 and also disconnect the panels from each other. Under direct sunlight with no shading, preferably around noon, measure the open circuit voltage of each solar panel. A normal reading should be above 42 VDC. If any panel shows a voltage significantly lower than 42 VDC, that solar panel is faulty and should be replaced.\nCheck the battery voltage\nDisconnect the battery from the TCS3 and measure battery voltage.\nIf the battery voltage is above 24 VDC, please proceed step 3.\nIf the voltage is below 22 VDC, use an external charger to charge the battery to above 24 VDC, then reconnect it to the TCS3 and continue test 3. If battery voltage is always below 22VDC even if fully charged, the batteries are defective and needs to be replaced.\nTest the TCS3 with solar panels disconnected\nKeep all solar panels disconnected and connect only the battery to the TCS3. Measure the voltage of BAT terminal and the LOAD terminal of the TCS3. The BAT terminal should read the approximately same as the battery voltage and the LOAD terminal should read above 22 VDC.\nIf the LOAD terminal voltage is below 22 VDC, the UPS01 is faulty.\nIf the BAT terminal voltage is below 22 VDC, replace the battery to have a try. If the problem remains, the TCS3 should be defective.\nIf both BAT and LOAD terminals show normal values, the TCS3 is good and you can proceed to Step 4.\nFinal test with solar panels connected\nReconnect the solar panels to the TCS3. Then measure the SOL terminal, BAT terminal, and LOAD terminal. Under normal operation, all three terminals should read approximately the same as the battery voltage. If any of these terminals shows an abnormal voltage, the solar panel should be faulty.",
