    "answer_en": "Please verify that the battery meet the required standards.\nGenerally, a 24V 12Ah battery (or 2pcs 12V 12Ah batteries connected in series may function as 24V) is required to power the gate opener. Lead acid / GEL / AGM / flooded (deep cycle) batteries can be used. Kindly note that the regulator is not compatible with most lithium-ion batteries, except for LiFePO4 batteries. And the battery should be waterproof type, or be placed in waterproof circumstance.\nMoreover, if you only use solar panels to charge the batteries (no AC electricity), you’re required to increase the solar panels power and the batteries capacity in the following situations:\nAdd continuously electricity-consuming accessories such as exit sensor wand, wired keypad, external receiver, etc. Normally, if you add such an accessory, you need to add 30W more solar panels.\nThere is less than 6 hours sunlight or the gate opener should be operated more than 10 cycles per day.\nThen check that all wiring is correct, especially the positive and negative connections and ensure  no loose or short-circuited connections are present.\nIf all above are verified, please disconnect any additional devices that may be powered by the same battery (e.g., auxiliary lights, access control readers, etc.).\nIf the battery is powering only the gate opener system, proceed to the next step.\nDisconnect all wired accessories and arm from the control board and leave only the main power input connected to the control board. If the problem persists, please move to step 4.\nTry another set of new batteries to have a try.\nIf the issue is resolved → The original battery is likely defective or has poor performance.\nIf the issue persists → Proceed to Step 5.\nDisconnect the TCS3 module from the control board. Leave the TCS3 connected only to the battery.\nIf abnormal drain continues → The TCS3 module is likely faulty and requires replacement.\nIf the drain stops → Proceed to Step 6.\nReconnect the TCS3 module to the control board. Ensure that no accessories and arm are connected to the control board (power only).\nIf the drain returns → The control board itself is likely faulty.\nIf there is no drain → The issue is caused by the arm or accessories. Reconnect arm and each accessory one by one to identify the faulty device.",
