    "answer_zh": "症状：换板后只朝一个方向/限位短接排查 · replaced control board · actuator direct 24V works · clicking remote no response · short DLMT COM ULMT limit switch · gate arm messed up won't work · only opens one direction motor runs both directions；非push remote 3 times·非must press remote multiple times·非remote needs multiple presses\n症状：机臂故障/限位短接/电机排查（bypassed motor limit switch jumping wires · short DLMT COM ULMT · gate arm messed up · only opens one direction；非gate does nothing push button·非opens too far limit B·非motor won't function lock unlocks only）\n症状：机臂故障/只朝一个方向/限位短接（gate arm messed up again · doesn't work at all · warranty arm replacement · A5131 · short DLMT COM ULMT · DIP switch 3 OFF · only opens one direction；非stops before opening fully·非opens too far into grass·非AT12131 limit screw B·非push remote 3 times）\n症状：机臂故障/只朝一个方向/限位短接（gate arm messed up again · doesn't work at all · warranty arm replacement · A5131 · short DLMT COM ULMT limit switch · DIP switch 3 OFF · only opens one direction · motor runs both directions limit defective；非开门过远opens too far·非完全不亮CODE LED）\n1 离合打开，把门推到中间试一试，判断是限位影响还是只朝一个方向转\n2 断开红外、关闭红外功能\n测电机\n4 短接限位\n没问题就是控制板坏\n如果判断是限位问题：\n单臂拉开门，只关不开，近端坏；只开不关，远端坏。\n单臂推开门，只关不开，远端坏；只开不关，近端坏。\n像有些不会/不愿换限位的，若确定是远端限位坏，可以只换远端限位。\n复杂方案：短接限位也只朝一个方向，换了控制板也不行\n测量一下继电器CLICK的时候MOTOR端口的电压，如果没电压那么肯定是控制板或限位有问题（可以通过短接限位端口排查限位）。如果正常有电压但是电机不动那么可以直接将电机线从控制板上取下，电机线直接接电池（红线接电池正、黑线接电池负电机朝一个方向运行，红线接电池负、黑线接电池正电机朝一个方向运行），看看电池带上电机后是否能正常朝两个方向运行，如果可以，那么可以分别测量一下电机运行时的电池电压和电机电流，看看电池压降（正常运行时电压不能降低到21VDC以下）和电机电流有没有异常（正常应该是1.2-6A）。",
    "answer_en": "1 Please release the clutch and push the gate to the middle position firstly. And then try it again by pressing the remote to see whether the gate can run towards the both directions. If the problem still persists, please do the following tests.\n2 Disconnect all wired accessories from the control board first (just leave the power source and the arm) and disable the photocell function by turning off DIP Switch 3#. Then press the remote again to see whether it can work properly.\nIf the problem persists, please do step 3.\nIf the problem disappears, reconnect each accessory one by one to identify which one causes the problem. If a photocell sensor is used, please double check the installation of the photocell, and make sure the photocell sensor beam is aligned and not blocked.\n3 Please check the motor. Connect the red & black wires of the arm to the DC 24V power source directly, the motor should run, and then exchange the polarity of the wires, the motor should run in the opposite direction. If the motor runs in both directions, the motor itself is good. Please connect the black & red wires back to the control board and check step4.\n4 Disconnect the BLUE, GREEN & YELLOW wires of the faulty arm from the control board, use two jumper wires to short the ULT, COM & DLT terminals to which the wires were connected, and then press the remote to see if the arm could extend and retract. If it could move in both directions, then the limit switch is defective. When you do this test, you could press the remote in time in case the arm extends too much.",
