    "answer_zh": "1 伸太过缩不回去的情况：\n离合打开，将机臂推到中间位置再合上离合再试，如果已经伸太过离合打开缩不回了，可尝试离合合上，顺时针往里边推边旋转拉杆，如果OK则说明之前丝母与丝杆之间脱开了（最远端），可以让客户将远端限位开关再往回调一点点，限位螺丝拧紧；如果还不行，需要拆机臂的话这一步可直接加入之前伸太过缩不回去的排查文章链接，让客人参考；\n2 拉杆在缩到底或部分伸出去的状态，电机转，机臂不伸缩：\n如果机臂拉杆推到中间位置，合上离合，电机依然只转，机臂不伸缩，说明问题可能在于机臂内部，离合或电机. 可以先检查离合是正确合上（拧到位），离合正常合上还不行，打开机臂再用离合钥匙开关离合，观察离合部位是否能正常啮合，如果不能，手动转下拉耳使其正常啮合；检查丝杆和带轴承的离合件3是否正常连接，拉杆螺母是否磨损，以上都正常的话可能是电机减速箱内部齿轮破损导致打滑。",
    "answer_en": "https://topens.com/blogs/blog-posts/troubleshooting-guide-motor-operates-but-gate-opener-arm-fails-to-move\n1 If the arm is stuck in the fully extended position and the moving-rod does not retract:\n(1) Disengage the clutch and manually push the moving-rod to the middle position. Then, press the remote control to test for movement.\n(2) If the arm still does not move, re-engage the clutch and detach the arm from the gate. While pushing the moving-rod inward, rotate the front mount clockwise. If the arm begins to move, the screw nut may have disengaged from the screw rod at the far end. Once the arm is back in the middle position, use the remote control to test operation again.\n(3) Once the arm functions properly, use a screwdriver to loosen the screw on Limit Switch B. Slide the switch slightly inward and re-tighten the screw to prevent future over-extension.\nFor additional guidance of the extended too much, please refer to this help article:\nhttps://topens.com/blogs/blog-posts/how-to-retract-the-moving-rod-when-the-opener-arm-extends-too-much\n2 If the opener arm is partially extended or fully retracted and the moving-rod does not move despite the motor activation:\n(1) Ensure that the clutch is fully and correctly engaged. If engagement appears normal, disassemble the opener arm and check whether clutch components (Part B and Part C) are properly aligned. If not, manually rotate the front mount until proper alignment is achieved.\n(2 ) Verify the connection between the screw rod and the clutch component with bearing (Part C). Also inspect the moving-rod’s screw nut for signs of damage or excessive wear.\n(3) If all visible components appear intact and operational, but abnormal or excessive noise is present in the motor area, the issue may lie within the motor’s reduction gearbox. Internal gear damage or slippage can prevent the arm from moving, even if the motor is running. In this case, please dismantle the gearbox of the motor and check the 