    "heading_level": 2,
    "answer_zh": "1. 打开离合，按遥控器，看是否还有异响？\n无异响→做步骤2；\n有异响→异响来自电机或离合，做步骤5；\n保持离合打开，手动开关门，看是否还有异响？\n无异响→异响很可能是由于电机负载过大产生；\n有异响→做步骤3；\n将机臂从门上取下，手动开关门，看是否还有异响？\n无异响→异响来自机臂前端，继续步骤4；\n有异响→问题在门（检查润滑门体、铰链等）\n保持离合打开，手动推拉伸缩杆，看是否顺畅丝滑。\n再合上离合，握住拉耳，按遥控器通电查看机臂是否有异响。\n如若卡顿或有异响，请润滑丝杆、丝母、外管、伸缩杆&挡圈。\n5.拆开外壳，保持主体完整，合上离合，按遥控器通电，确认异响来自哪里？\n离合件凸轮刮擦产生的异响→在摩擦部位加润滑脂；\n电机内部异响→齿轮箱的问题，更换齿轮箱。",
    "answer_en": "Release the clutch and press the remote to run the opener.\nIf the noise disappears, please proceed to Step 2.\nIf the noise remains, it likely comes from the motor or clutch. In this case, please go directly to Step 5.\nKeep the clutch released and try opening and closing the gate by hand.\nIf the noise is gone, the issue is likely caused by excessive motor load when the gate is connected. Please check for gate obstructions and verify that the gate does not exceed the opener's rated capacity.\nIf the noise persists, please move on to Step 3.\nDetach the actuator arm from the gate then manually open and close the gate again.\nIf the noise stops, the problem is likely coming from the front part of the actuator arm. Please continue to Step 4.\nIf the noise continues, the issue is with the gate itself. Please check and lubricate hinges of the gate to ensure smooth operation.\nKeep the clutch disengaged and the arm removed from the gate, manually push and pull the moving-rod. It should move smoothly without resistance.\nThen engage the clutch, hold the front mount, and press the remote to power the actuator while listening carefully for any noise.\nIf you feel sticking or hear unusual noise, please lubricate the arm.\nSpray WD40 or the ordinary engine oil on the stainless steel moving-rod\nDismantle the arm and lubricate the inside including the screw rod, nut, and the outer tube.\nHow to lubricate inside of the arm\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IRIA5iaWHqE\nEngage the clutch, open the outer housing of the arm and inspect the internal components. Then press the remote to make the arm run again while listening carefully to locate the source of the noise.\nIf the noise comes from the clutch cam scraping against other parts, apply grease to the friction area.\nIf the noise comes from inside the motor, the gearbox may be faulty. In this case, please replace the gearbox.\nThe pictures of how removing the outer housing for your reference.",
